messages.content:
I see the issue. The Modal component uses `<script setup>` but tries to access `this.$refs.dialogRef` in the `<script>` section, which won't work. The `dialogRef` needs to be properly exposed. Let me fix this:

```vue src/components/Modal.vue
<script setup>
import { ref } from 'vue'
</script>

<template>
  <dialog
    :id="id"
    ref="dialogRef"
    class="modal modal-bottom sm:modal-middle"
    @click="handleBackdropClick"
    @cancel="handleClose"
  >
    <div class="modal-box w-full sm:max-w-2xl">
      <!-- Header -->
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
        <slot name="header">
          <span class="text-lg font-semibold text-base-content"></span>
        </slot>
        <button
          v-if="close"
          class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm btn-circle text-base-content/60 hover:text-error transition-colors"
          @click="handleClose"
        >
          <i class="fa-solid fa-xmark text-lg"></i>
        </button>
      </div>

      <!-- Body -->
      <div class="py-4">
        <slot></slot>
      </div>

      <!-- Footer -->
      <div v-if="$slots.footer" class="modal-action">
        <slot name="footer"></slot>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Backdrop -->
    <form method="dialog" class="modal-backdrop">
      <button v-if="dismissable" type="button"></button>
    </form>
  </dialog>
</template>

<script>
export default {
  props: {
    id: {
      type: String,
      required: true
    },
    close: {
      type: Boolean,
      default: true
    },
    dismissable: {
      type: Boolean,
      default: true
    },
    scope: String
  },
  emits: ['close'],
  data() {
    return {
      dialogRef: null
    }
  },
  mounted() {
    this.dialogRef = this.$refs.dialogRef
  },
  methods: {
    open() {
      this.dialogRef?.showModal()
    },
    closeModal() {
      this.dialogRef?.close()
      this.$emit('close')
    },
    handleClose() {
      this.closeModal()
    },
    handleBackdropClick(e) {
      if (this.dismissable && e.target === this.dialogRef) {
        this.handleClose()
      }
    }
  }
}
</script>
```

## Changes Summary

| Change | Details |
|--------|---------|
| **Added mounted hook** | Assigns `this.$refs.dialogRef` to `this.dialogRef` data property |
| **Fixed ref access** | Changed `this.$refs.dialogRef?.showModal()` to `this.dialogRef?.showModal()` |
| **Fixed backdrop click** | Changed `this.$refs.dialogRef` to `this.dialogRef` in `handleBackdropClick` |
| **Proper data binding** | Now dialogRef is properly accessible in all methods |

**What was wrong:**
- The `<script setup>` defines `dialogRef` as a ref variable but it's not exported to the `<script>` section
- The `<script>` section couldn't access the template ref properly
- Solution: Access it once in `mounted` and store in data property for consistent access

The Modal should now display correctly when `open()` is called!
